      "text": "CBP agriculture specialists in Detroit intercepted an invasive grain pest that is quarantine significant. Thanks to specialized training and vigilance, a traveler was referred to secondary inspection when seeds for growing purposes were found in their luggage. Inside the bag was a single cast skin, confirmed by the USDA as belonging to the khapra beetle.  Our team is frontline safeguarding our economy and environment from dangerous pests and diseases.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/2MbmR8T8vT",
